<%# The spec asks for a remaining amount that is always visible, so it reads the
    same whether it is zero or not: the organizer should never have to wonder
    whether the line is missing or the figure is nil.

    In custom mode this is the number being worked down to zero, and it is what
    keeps the total honest now that the sliders themselves are unrestrained. It
    can read either way: "Left to give" when the rows come to less than the bill,
    "Over by" when they come to more. SplitLogic updates both on every drag. %>
<% remaining_cents = split.remaining_cents %>

<div id="remaining" class="mt-4 border-t-2 border-black pt-3">
  <p class="flex items-baseline justify-between">
    <span class="font-medium" data-split-logic-target="remainingLabel">
      <%= remaining_cents.negative? ? "Over by" : "Left to give" %>
    </span>
    <span class="font-medium tabular-nums" data-split-logic-target="remaining">
      <%= money(remaining_cents.abs) %>
    </span>
  </p>

  <% if split.custom? %>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-black/60">
      Every share has to be given out before you can save.
    </p>
  <% end %>
</div>
